    "diagnosis": "BIOMASS_ABOVE_READING",
    "late_biomass_estimate_od": 2.7,
    "p_biomass_above_reading": 0.98,
    "rationale": "The undiluted readings stop at about 0.76 from hour 5 to hour 18. That flat plateau after fast exponential growth looks like detector saturation. I tested the 18 h aliquot at two dilutions. At 10x it read 0.261, which scales to about 2.61. At 25x it read 0.108, which scales to about 2.69. The two dilution-corrected values agree with each other, and both are about 3.5 times the undiluted reading of 0.75. The undiluted reading therefore underestimates the biomass. The 25x reading is the less nonlinear of the two, so I estimate the true OD at 18 h at about 2.7. Each dilution was read once because of the budget, so there is no replicate-based error estimate."
  },
